{
  "dom_id": "step-t8191",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Recall that two variables, $x$ and $y,$ are said to have a proportional relationship if their ratio is constant. The constant of proportionality $k$ is given by\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the equation above as follows:\n\n$$\ny = kx\n$$\n\nThe following statements are all equivalent:\n\n- $y = kx$\n\n- $y$ **varies directly** with $x$\n\n- $y$ is **directly proportional** to $x$\n\n- $y \\propto x$\n\nProportional relationships frequently occur in real-world problems. Let's see an example.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
